Ze-Reviewed-Against: github.com/openconfig/goyang v1.6.4-0.20251113201521-a80f2799d7b9

goyang numbers an enum member with no value after a negative value from 0,
against RFC 7950 Section 9.6.4.2: "If a value is not specified, then one will
be automatically assigned. If the "enum" substatement is the first one
defined, the assigned value is zero (0); otherwise, the assigned value is one
greater than the current highest enum value (i.e., the highest enum value,
implicit or explicit, prior to the current "enum" substatement in the parent
"type" statement)". It then refuses valid modules
with a duplicate value. Proposed upstream as
https://github.com/openconfig/goyang/pull/317. Delete this patch once the
goyang release go.mod requires contains that fix.

Design: docs/contributing/patching-the-standard-library.md, "Patching a vendored
module".

diff --git a/vendor/github.com/openconfig/goyang/pkg/yang/types_builtin.go b/vendor/github.com/openconfig/goyang/pkg/yang/types_builtin.go
--- a/vendor/github.com/openconfig/goyang/pkg/yang/types_builtin.go
+++ b/vendor/github.com/openconfig/goyang/pkg/yang/types_builtin.go
@@ -619,11 +619,14 @@ func (e *EnumType) Set(name string, value int64) error {
 	if value > e.max {
 		return fmt.Errorf("value %d for %s too large (maximum is %d)", value, name, e.max)
 	}
-	e.ToString[value] = name
-	e.ToInt[name] = value
-	if value >= e.last {
+	// RFC 7950 section 9.6.4.2: an implicit value is one greater than the
+	// highest value assigned so far, whether that value is negative or not.
+	// The initial last of -1 only makes the first implicit value zero.
+	if len(e.ToInt) == 0 || value > e.last {
 		e.last = value
 	}
+	e.ToString[value] = name
+	e.ToInt[name] = value
 	return nil
 }
 
